1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,800
Four ways to buy gold on MCX.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,500
Same gold. Which price is fair?

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,800
Per gram of pure gold, they almost match.

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,900
Meet Parity: MCX gold futures intelligence. A guided tour in 8 short stops.

5
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:24,050
This is Parity. Each page answers one simple question about MCX gold futures.

6
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,750
Any dotted word explains itself. Just hover over it.

7
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:34,450
Every page opens with the answer first, in the In short box.

8
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,783
The latest closing prices, all four turned into ₹ per gram of pure gold.

9
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:44,583
Premium = how much dearer than GOLDM. Usual = its normal level.

10
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:51,183
Today all sit near their usual level, so the signal is quiet. No noise.

11
00:00:51,233 --> 00:00:56,417
Every table downloads as a spreadsheet, ready for Excel.

12
00:00:56,467 --> 00:01:00,417
Lost? Press Ctrl + K and search the whole site.

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:10,917
The organisers asked for five things. Each card: the ask, what we built, a link to the proof.

14
00:01:10,967 --> 00:01:16,083
All five are done, and every line of the final challenge is answered.

15
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:23,117
Here we compare contracts two at a time, per gram of pure gold.

16
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:30,050
GOLDM vs GOLDTEN: the line hugs zero. Same gold, same price. Our maths checks out.

17
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:35,783
GOLDM vs the 8 g coin: the coin is always dearer, about 60 bp (0.6%) per gram.

18
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:40,450
In the Dec 2025 – Mar 2026 crash that gap blew out past 2.6%.

19
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:45,483
Dearer in all 41 contract months: a lasting premium, not a mistake.

20
00:01:47,767 --> 00:01:52,250
Each dot is one contract. Further right = it expires later.

21
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:59,283
Later costs more, like rent for holding gold until then. That's the cost of carry.

22
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:07,483
90 days back the whole line sat elsewhere: gold itself moved, not just time.

23
00:02:07,533 --> 00:02:13,350
Time alone moves GOLDM only about 0.6% a month. Gold's own moves are far bigger.

24
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:21,050
The big question: buy the cheap one, sell the dear one. Do you make money?

25
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:26,517
Slippage is the bit you lose each time an order fills. With perfect fills…

26
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:31,917
…profit looks big. At 10 bp most of it vanishes. Costs decide everything.

27
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:37,217
So every result is shown at 5 bp, the realistic middle.

28
00:02:37,267 --> 00:02:44,483
Strategy A's profit came almost all from one crash month: January 2026.

29
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:50,917
Strategy B, the fair-price rule: fewer trades, steadier, still positive.

30
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:56,217
Most backtests skip costs and grade a rule on the data it was tuned on…

31
00:02:56,267 --> 00:03:01,183
…so the numbers look huge. That is not real money.

32
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:06,417
Ours: real costs, on data the rules had never seen.

33
00:03:06,467 --> 00:03:12,517
The hardest exam: 8 more years (2016–2023), locked away until the rules were frozen.

34
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:19,883
Strategy A failed. Strategy B made money in both windows. Small, but real.

35
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:25,483
A bet on gold going up? No. Every trade's profit is split into gap and gold.

36
00:03:27,767 --> 00:03:33,383
Is any contract far from its fair price right now? The black marker is today.

37
00:03:33,433 --> 00:03:39,350
Past the red ticks an alert fires. Today every contract is normal.

38
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:48,183
66 alerts since 2023. A typical one saw the gap close 51 bp within 10 trading days.

39
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:54,517
Every alert is on record with what happened next. Most days, the honest answer is: wait.

40
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:02,750
Each bar is one contract, from its first trading day to expiry.

41
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:11,817
Each dash is a trade: green made money, red lost. The pink band is the 2026 crash.

42
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:18,050
The dark end of each bar is the run-up to delivery. Strategy B always exits before it.

43
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:27,817
Built on 723 official MCX files: 12,021 rows checked, 0 unexplained errors.

44
00:04:27,867 --> 00:04:35,150
Rules like the delivery period come straight from MCX's own documents.

45
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:39,350
And for late nights, a dark mode.

46
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:46,800
What you just saw: a fair comparison, the curve explained, honest backtests, 8 sealed years, quiet alerts, and the contract calendar.

47
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:50,800
The honest answer: a small, real edge. Tested honestly, doubts included.

48
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:54,800
Parity by SYNTAX TERROR (TAN): Nikhil Kumar, Sai Ganesh, Ishaan Chhabra.
